## The ollama class contacts the server in its constructor, so an object cannot
## be built without one and only the two branches that raise before that call
## are reachable offline.  Everything else in the class is exercised against a
## live server.
%!error<ollama: unsupported mode option 'bogus'.> ollama ('http://127.0.0.1:1', '', 'bogus')
%!error<ollama: invalid serverURL input.> ollama (42)
%!error<ollama: invalid serverURL input.> ollama ({'http://127.0.0.1:1'})
